{"id":53,"text":"Tom was proud when he became an apprentice to the village blacksmith. But after a month, he was disappointed. Every day, the blacksmith only asked him to make nails, and Tom thought that was boring.\n\n“When will I make something important?” he complained. “Swords? Armour? Tools for the king?”\n\nThe blacksmith said nothing. He just continued working.\n\nOne morning, a soldier came to the shop in a hurry. “My horse has lost a shoe,” he said. “I must reach the castle today. The king is in danger!”\n\nThe blacksmith looked at Tom. “Make a horseshoe,” he said. “Quickly.”\n\nTom’s hands moved by themselves. He heated the iron, shaped it and cooled it. He fixed the shoe to the horse’s foot in less than ten minutes.\n\nThe soldier thanked them and galloped away. Later, the village heard that he had arrived on time and saved the king’s life.\n\nThat evening, Tom sat next to his master. “Thank you,” he said quietly. “I understand now. Making all those nails taught me to work fast and well.”\n\nThe blacksmith nodded. “Small tasks prepare you for big moments,” he said. “You never know when your time will come.”\n\nMoral: Every small task you do well is preparation for something great.","tr":null,"gl":{"tom":"Tom (ism)","was":"edi","proud":"faxrlangan, mag'rur","when":"qachon; -ganda","he":"u (erkak)","became":"bo'lib qoldi","an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","apprentice":"shogird","to":"-ga; uchun","the":"(aniq artikl)","village":"qishloq","blacksmith":"temirchi","but":"lekin, ammo","after":"keyin, so'ng","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","month":"oy","disappointed":"hafsalasi pir bo'lgan","every":"har","day":"kun","only":"faqat, yagona","asked":"so'radi","him":"uni, unga","make":"qilmoq, yasamoq","nails":"mixlar","and":"va","thought":"o'yladi; fikr","that":"u, o'sha; -ki","boring":"zerikarli","will":"-adi (kelasi zamon)","i":"men","something":"nimadir","important":"muhim","complained":"shikoyat qildi","swords":"qilichlar","armour":"sovut","tools":"asboblar","for":"uchun; da